+## Stored shuffle order (proposed desktop behaviour)
+
+The displayed queue stays in source order. The playback order is held in memory for the current
+session. "Once" means once per queue entry; duplicate track ids remain separate entries.
+
+| ID | Given | When | Then | Desktop | Android |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| SHUF-01 | A finite queue, shuffle on | Advance through one pass | Each queue entry is visited once. Repeat off stops at the end; repeat on wraps through the same permutation. | yes | verify |
+| SHUF-02 | Shuffle on | Previous or direct track selection | Previous follows the stored order with TR-01/TR-02. Direct selection moves the cursor to that entry in the order. | yes | verify |
+| SHUF-03 | A track is playing or paused | Switch shuffle | Current audio, position and pause state stay unchanged. Enabling starts a new permutation with the current track first. Disabling uses source order. | yes | verify |
+| SHUF-04 | Shuffle on | Append, insert or remove queue entries | Rebuild the permutation from the current entry; a new pass can include previously heard entries. Removing the current entry retains the existing stop behaviour. An empty queue stays stopped. | yes | verify |
+| SHUF-05 | Shuffle on | Preload, manual Next or gapless advance | All use the same next entry. Preload lookahead does not advance the cursor; it advances only when that entry becomes current. | yes | verify |
+| SHUF-06 | Shuffle on | A wave starts, or an ordinary queue replaces it | WAVE-10/WAVE-11 apply; no stored shuffle order is used in a wave. | yes | yes |
